<node>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="A decimal fraction number written as floating-point number. The standard type used internally is double with 64 Bits. It has a value range from 2^−1022 to approximately 2^1024, which is from 2 × 10^−308 to 2 × 10^308. CAUTION! The cybol parser is able to recognise many variants, with small or capital letter E, with or without plus sign, as shown in the examples below. However, the RECOMMENDED FORM is as follows: 1.23E+4 The plus sign of the number is OPTIONAL. The plus sign of the scientific notation exponent is MANDATORY."/>
    <node name="examples" channel="file" format="text/plain" model="api-generator/spec/state/number/fraction-decimal/examples.txt"/>
</node>
